{
  "Name": "Zabbix Authenticated Remote Command Execution",
  "Description": "ZABBIX allows an administrator to create scripts that will be run on hosts. An authenticated attacker can create a script containing a payload, then a host with an IP of 127.0.0.1 and run the arbitrary script on the ZABBIX host. This module was tested against Zabbix v2.0.9, v2.0.5, v3.0.1, v4.0.18, v5.0.17, v6.0.0.",
